86045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072913 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "65ec0190-043b-57d7-91de-b1b25e2d321b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073415 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10542" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073415 #edb/ref 1071 "Greg stacked $5$ cardboard boxes on top of each other. How tall was his pile if each box is $\\dfrac{3}{4}\\,\\textrm{ft}$ high?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073415 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3deda9a1-7edd-5b1e-9f39-5c69644f30ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073415 #edb/ref 1074 "To find out the height of the pile of boxes, we have to multiply\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nby $5$.\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n5 \\times \\dfrac34 = \\dfrac{5\\times 3}{4} = \\dfrac{15}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {15}{4}\n$$\n\nto a mixed number:\n\n$$\n15 \\div 4 = 3\\,\\textrm{R}\\,3 = 3\\,\\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nSo, Greg's stack of boxes was\n\n$$\n3\\,\\dfrac{3}{4}\\,\\textrm{ft}\n$$\n\nhigh." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073416 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10543" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073416 #edb/ref 1071 "Mr. Stewart spends $\\dfrac56$ hours watching an episode of his favorite TV show. If $5$ episodes are played every week, find the total time he spends watching the show every week. Between what two whole numbers does your answer lie?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073416 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9fb671f7-6d04-5863-9683-3b2c3753df73" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073416 #edb/ref 1074 "To find out how long Mr. Stewart watches the show each week, we need to multiply\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{6}\n$$\n\nby $5$.\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n5\\times\\dfrac56 = \\dfrac{5\\times 5}{6} = \\dfrac{25}6\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {25}{6}\n$$\n\nto a mixed number:\n\n$$\n25 \\div 6 = 4\\,\\textrm{R}\\,1 = 4\\,\\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSo, Mr. Stewart spends a total of\n\n$$\n4\\,\\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nhours watching the show, which lies between $4$ and $5$ hours." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073538 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1863" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073538 #edb/ref 1071 "Larry filled his water bottle with $12\\, \\mathrm{oz}$ of drinking water. If he drank $\\dfrac34$ of the bottle's contents after exercising, how much water did Larry drink?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073538 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "737b03c4-95f0-5a89-a428-e051b9efee6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073538 #edb/ref 1074 "To find out how much water Larry drank, we need to multiply $12$ by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac34 \\times 12 = \\dfrac{3\\times 12}{4} = \\dfrac{36}4\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{36}{4} = 36 \\div 4=9\n$$\n\nSo, Larry drank $9\\,\\textrm{oz}$ of water." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1039 "Multiplying a Fraction by a Whole Number: Result Is a Mixed Number" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073415 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073793 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "940366ef-28e8-5827-b52d-a8b500dbb2a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073794 #edb/ref 1039 "Determining Whole Number Bounds of a Multiplication Problem" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073794 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073794 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b58f3a78-53