069 "q-60472" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074445 #edb/ref 1071 "A wooden slat is $3ft$ long. Eddie needs to cut a piece that's $\\frac{5}{8}$ the length of the slat. How long is the piece he has to cut?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074445 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7aec9a99-287b-5359-b077-2d2284acc8d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074734 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074734 #edb/ref 1061 39848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074734 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f5e9fd25-c8c7-5c5a-a339-898928ef9262" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074734 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074735 #edb/ref 1061 39849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074735 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c28fe622-ab99-50b0-a92e-6e1e1322ca4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074735 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074837 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074837 #edb/ref 1061 6461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074837 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "96933400-d1d9-564b-821e-12dd6c004ad6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074837 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186074957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074838 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074838 #edb/ref 1061 6462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074838 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e1f36309-f225-55f2-a168-85f87992f190" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074838 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074957 #edb/ref 1064 "In this lesson, we'll consider real-life situations where we have to multiply fractions by whole numbers.\n\nSuppose that Justin, a chef, has $8$ large tins of tomatoes. If each tin of tomatoes weighs\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{4}\\,\\textrm{lb}\n$$\n\nhow many pounds of tomatoes does Justin have in total?\n\nTo find out the total weight of tomatoes, we need to multiply\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{4}\\,\\textrm{lb}\n$$\n\nby $8$.\n\nTo multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n8 \\times \\dfrac54= \\dfrac{8\\times 5}{4} = \\dfrac{40}4\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this fraction by interpreting the fraction as a division:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{40}{4} = 40 \\div 4 = 10\n$$\n\nSo, in total, Justin has $10\\,\\textrm{lb}$ of tomatoes." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074957 #edb/ref 1065 1886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074957 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "298ab81d-8afe-5255-bdcd-354d669f8700" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074957 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
